1
00:00:01,016 --> 00:00:03,063
A Fantastic Duo

2
00:00:05,799 --> 00:00:07,480
Your lemon water.

3
00:00:08,425 --> 00:00:09,894
Hey, Blaion?

4
00:00:09,894 --> 00:00:10,384
Hm? 

5
00:00:10,384 --> 00:00:12,192
What should we call the relationship between us?

6
00:00:12,192 --> 00:00:13,525
What's this all of a sudden?

7
00:00:13,525 --> 00:00:17,161
Jun said that the Metal Cardbots are his friends.

8
00:00:17,161 --> 00:00:21,713
He also said that even if you were born on different planets, if your hearts make a connection, you can become friends. 

9
00:00:21,713 --> 00:00:25,227
Is our reason for working together only because we provide some kind of value for each other?

10
00:00:25,227 --> 00:00:26,719
Maybe.

11
00:00:26,719 --> 00:00:30,065
Will I ever get to call you a friend?

12
00:00:30,065 --> 00:00:32,045
I don't care what you decide to call me.

13
00:00:32,045 --> 00:00:35,621
Just think about what you can do in preparation for the promised day.

14
00:00:35,621 --> 00:00:36,960
...Okay.

15
00:00:38,002 --> 00:00:39,487
Here! Pass! Pass!

16
00:00:39,487 --> 00:00:40,750
Okay! Here goes!

17
00:00:40,750 --> 00:00:42,088
- GRRAA!!
- Hurry up, man!

18
00:00:45,286 --> 00:00:46,518
Here, Vance!

19
00:00:47,521 --> 00:00:50,456
Tigun! Be careful not to hurt the kids!

20
00:00:50,456 --> 00:00:52,753
That's one enthusiastic Metal Cardbot.

21
00:00:52,753 --> 00:00:54,154
Wild Cardbot.

22
00:00:54,154 --> 00:00:55,484
Aren't they all the same?

23
00:00:55,484 --> 00:01:00,548
When they were all living on planet Machina, Metal Cardbots and Wild Cardbots were enemies to each other.

24
00:01:00,548 --> 00:01:05,387
But Machina is gone now. Now is the time for us to work together to forge a new future.

25
00:01:05,387 --> 00:01:07,301
What are you gonna do about that flying bot, though?

26
00:01:07,301 --> 00:01:09,971
Ugh. You mean Night Griffon, right?

27
00:01:09,971 --> 00:01:13,837
I think he's still hiding somewhere around town, but it's hard to find him.

28
00:01:13,837 --> 00:01:16,075
I'm more worried about the Beast Virus.

29
00:01:16,075 --> 00:01:21,222
I heard Crest is coming over today to tell us about the vaccine, so I'd assume there's at least some progress.

30
00:01:21,722 --> 00:01:23,298
What is he, a cat?

31
00:01:23,298 --> 00:01:25,745
He said looking at the ball stirs his wild instincts.

32
00:01:25,745 --> 00:01:27,923
You tamed him well.

33
00:01:27,923 --> 00:01:29,620
I assume you used the power of the Metal Breath?

34
00:01:29,620 --> 00:01:30,765
No, I didn't.

35
00:01:30,765 --> 00:01:33,212
Jun and Tigun became friends.

36
00:01:33,212 --> 00:01:35,621
Hmph. Again with that nonsense.

37
00:01:36,103 --> 00:01:37,033
Lavi!

38
00:01:39,670 --> 00:01:40,692
Watch out!

39
00:01:44,115 --> 00:01:47,682
You became friends with a menace like him? What a miserable joke!

40
00:01:47,682 --> 00:01:49,206
What?! You wanna fight or something?!

41
00:01:49,206 --> 00:01:50,621
That's enough, Tigun.

42
00:01:50,621 --> 00:01:52,002
Grrrr!!

43
00:01:52,301 --> 00:01:55,331
Night Griffon must be hiding somewhere in town.

44
00:01:55,331 --> 00:01:56,063
How about we work together to-

45
00:01:56,063 --> 00:01:57,533
I decline.

46
00:01:57,533 --> 00:01:58,948
Soleil!

47
00:01:58,948 --> 00:02:01,649
I'm the one who will capture Night Griffon.

48
00:02:01,649 --> 00:02:02,405
Hey!

49
00:02:02,405 --> 00:02:05,665
Ugh. She's so cold, we can't even talk to her.

50
00:02:05,665 --> 00:02:07,426
Not much of a social butterfly, huh.

51
00:02:07,426 --> 00:02:10,443
She's nothing like Crest. Are they really twins?

52
00:02:10,443 --> 00:02:11,764
Just forget her.

53
00:02:11,764 --> 00:02:14,985
No. I'll make her change her mind no matter what!

54
00:02:15,288 --> 00:02:16,554
Wait!

55
00:02:16,554 --> 00:02:17,173
What is it?

56
00:02:17,173 --> 00:02:19,646
How are you going to find Night Griffon?

57
00:02:19,646 --> 00:02:23,021
This photo was taken at the stadium. Let's work together to find him using this photo as a clue.

58
00:02:23,021 --> 00:02:24,954
That's useless as a clue.

59
00:02:24,954 --> 00:02:26,115
Then how about this?

60
00:02:26,115 --> 00:02:27,626
- Then how about this?
- [Mr. Jim! Isn't that him?]

61
00:02:27,626 --> 00:02:29,115
- [Oh! That's the one I saw when I was at the landfill with the kids!]

62
00:02:29,115 --> 00:02:31,609
- [Oh! That's the one I saw when I was at the landfill with the kids!]
- This footage doesn't tell us where he is either.

63
00:02:31,609 --> 00:02:33,491
Then... how about this? 

64
00:02:33,491 --> 00:02:39,180
This is data on explosion sounds recorded by a noise meter installed on a single-lane road. We'll be able to track his flight path using this data.

65
00:02:39,180 --> 00:02:42,670
The city hall has received several complaints about airplane noise lately, too.

66
00:02:42,670 --> 00:02:48,538
Night Griffon's top speed is Mach 7. He's fast enough to cross this town in the blink of an eye. How are you going to catch him?

67
00:02:48,538 --> 00:02:52,697
That's why we're asking for some cooperation! If we work together, we can beat anyone no matter how strong-

68
00:02:52,697 --> 00:02:53,968
Sounds to me like you have no plan whatsoever.

69
00:02:53,968 --> 00:02:54,906
What?!

70
00:02:54,906 --> 00:02:56,143
Are you always like this?

71
00:02:56,143 --> 00:02:56,901
Will you please stop-!

72
00:02:56,901 --> 00:02:59,137
Ahahaha... Don't fight, guys.

73
00:02:59,137 --> 00:03:00,366
What's goin' on over here?? Is there a fight??

74
00:03:00,366 --> 00:03:01,465
Tigun! Stop!

75
00:03:01,465 --> 00:03:05,074
I, Tigun, the strongest Wild Cardbot, will fight for you!

76
00:03:05,074 --> 00:03:08,592
Bzz! Says the big buffoon who rolls around in the dirt! What do you know about being the strongest?!

77
00:03:08,592 --> 00:03:10,139
What didja say?!?! Come on out of there and fight me!!

78
00:03:10,139 --> 00:03:12,425
Now we're talking! Soleil!

79
00:03:12,425 --> 00:03:13,586
Are you really trying to fight me now!?

80
00:03:13,586 --> 00:03:14,562
If I must.

81
00:03:15,199 --> 00:03:16,818
Phantom Hornet. Set Up.

82
00:03:20,198 --> 00:03:22,009
Tigun! Set Up!

83
00:03:38,574 --> 00:03:39,913
Everyone, please calm down!

84
00:03:39,913 --> 00:03:42,454
Jun, if you act like this, it'll make us look bad!

85
00:03:42,454 --> 00:03:45,247
The school and the townsfolk will be in danger if we fight here...

86
00:03:45,247 --> 00:03:46,352
I know that!

87
00:03:46,352 --> 00:03:50,372
Soleil, let's talk this out for the sake of my kind. Please!

88
00:03:50,372 --> 00:03:51,311
Be quiet.

89
00:03:55,311 --> 00:03:56,573
Oh-ho...

90
00:04:06,038 --> 00:04:10,132
You lot are finally doing something entertaining. I was getting tired of waiting.

91
00:04:10,132 --> 00:04:11,806
Night Griffon!

92
00:04:11,806 --> 00:04:14,146
I'd quite like to join the fun, if you wouldn't mind.

93
00:04:14,146 --> 00:04:15,235
You again?!

94
00:04:15,235 --> 00:04:17,302
Sounds like you wanna feel the sting, too!

95
00:04:17,302 --> 00:04:21,026
Heh heh! My Crimson Lance also packs quite a sting!

96
00:04:23,754 --> 00:04:24,752
Got you!

97
00:04:27,317 --> 00:04:28,862
My my, aren't you slow.

98
00:04:28,862 --> 00:04:30,848
Dang it. I can't move...!

99
00:04:31,427 --> 00:04:32,754
Did the virus get them?

100
00:04:32,754 --> 00:04:34,110
I thought they were immune to it?!

101
00:04:34,110 --> 00:04:36,413
But I was able to move after he stabbed me with the same thing!

102
00:04:36,413 --> 00:04:37,786
- Hey, you!
- Stop this now!

103
00:04:37,987 --> 00:04:40,293
Hmph! What a banal attack!

104
00:04:40,293 --> 00:04:41,480
Tigun! Come back!

105
00:04:41,480 --> 00:04:43,201
Soleil, I'll go this time.

106
00:04:43,521 --> 00:04:45,173
Blaion. Set Up.

107
00:04:58,379 --> 00:05:01,569
Heheheh! Finally, a worthy opponent!

108
00:05:01,569 --> 00:05:04,120
You think this is some kind of game?

109
00:05:04,550 --> 00:05:06,596
Won't you ever grow up?!

110
00:05:06,596 --> 00:05:09,338
Do yourself a favor and YOU grow up instead.

111
00:05:10,213 --> 00:05:12,540
I'll be having fun for the rest of my life!

112
00:05:15,201 --> 00:05:17,617
Jun, shouldn't we help him?

113
00:05:17,617 --> 00:05:20,485
I think we should call a truce for a while. Let's work together!

114
00:05:20,485 --> 00:05:20,994
Why?

115
00:05:20,994 --> 00:05:24,521
You still don't get it?! We can't beat him if we face him one-on-one!

116
00:05:24,521 --> 00:05:27,538
I'll handle him on my own. Blaion. Leon Roar Shot.

117
00:05:29,012 --> 00:05:29,730
Hah!

118
00:05:46,235 --> 00:05:47,033
Blaion!

119
00:05:47,533 --> 00:05:48,807
Let me go now!

120
00:05:49,108 --> 00:05:50,310
As you wish.

121
00:05:54,737 --> 00:05:57,478
Now, it's about time I put an end to this!

122
00:05:57,987 --> 00:05:58,747
He's coming down!

123
00:05:58,747 --> 00:05:59,887
Blaion, get up!

124
00:05:59,887 --> 00:06:01,062
I know!

125
00:06:02,309 --> 00:06:04,605
Scream Of Talon!

126
00:06:05,156 --> 00:06:07,374
Fire Roar Blaze!

127
00:06:07,374 --> 00:06:09,216
Fire Roar... 

128
00:06:09,516 --> 00:06:10,848
Blaze!

129
00:06:13,009 --> 00:06:14,389
He's at a disadvantage when he's in the air.

130
00:06:14,389 --> 00:06:17,360
He's going to fall! Soleil! You need to get out of there!

131
00:06:17,360 --> 00:06:19,514
You really are one of a kind.

132
00:06:19,514 --> 00:06:22,586
But at the end of the day, you're still just a ground dwelling kitty under an eagle's wing!

133
00:06:22,586 --> 00:06:23,543
Hurry up!

134
00:06:24,689 --> 00:06:26,490
Oh no...! Get out of here, guys!

135
00:06:31,677 --> 00:06:32,826
Jun! Are you okay?!

136
00:06:32,826 --> 00:06:34,045
Soleil just-!

137
00:06:34,497 --> 00:06:35,689
Phoenix Fire!

138
00:06:35,689 --> 00:06:37,298
Ar... are you alright...?

139
00:06:37,298 --> 00:06:41,288
You... Did you just save me? Even while knowing you'd be injured during the process?

140
00:06:41,288 --> 00:06:44,658
It's only natural for a rescue worker to save people in crisis... right...?

141
00:06:44,658 --> 00:06:45,557
I don't understand.

142
00:06:45,557 --> 00:06:49,411
And... I know that if something happened to you... Jun would be very sad...

143
00:06:49,411 --> 00:06:50,199
What?

144
00:06:53,180 --> 00:06:54,939
Phoenix Fire... is that...?!

145
00:06:54,939 --> 00:06:59,225
Well well well, isn't this unflattering. Did I get too excited?

146
00:07:00,576 --> 00:07:02,673
It feels like my body is burning...!!

147
00:07:02,673 --> 00:07:03,903
Phoenix Fire!!

148
00:07:03,903 --> 00:07:06,788
Oh, my. Looks like my lance hit the wrong individual.

149
00:07:06,987 --> 00:07:08,100
Blue Cop! Set Up!

150
00:07:15,603 --> 00:07:16,557
That must be...

151
00:07:16,557 --> 00:07:18,237
The Beast Virus!

152
00:07:18,237 --> 00:07:22,661
Soleil! Please, you have to help him! You fixed Blue Cop before!

153
00:07:22,661 --> 00:07:24,548
You did say he's... your dear friend...

154
00:07:24,548 --> 00:07:28,954
No! I won't allow it! Soleil's life will be in danger if she pulls that stunt again!

155
00:07:28,954 --> 00:07:29,939
But...!!

156
00:07:33,119 --> 00:07:39,011
Haha... Given how well he's holding up during the transformation process, he's sure to become quite an interesting opponent once it's complete!

157
00:07:39,673 --> 00:07:42,175
Blue Cop! Throw me onto that building!

158
00:07:42,175 --> 00:07:43,793
Wild Guardy! Mega Ambler!

159
00:07:49,139 --> 00:07:50,911
Jun! Give me power!

160
00:07:50,911 --> 00:07:52,798
Uh... got it!

161
00:07:52,798 --> 00:07:53,733
What is all this?

162
00:07:54,500 --> 00:07:55,257
Stay still!

163
00:07:55,557 --> 00:07:57,636
Wild Guardy! Set Up!

164
00:07:57,636 --> 00:08:00,129
Wild Calibur!!

165
00:08:02,752 --> 00:08:03,869
Mega Ambler! Hurry!!

166
00:08:03,869 --> 00:08:04,954
Crest!

167
00:08:05,658 --> 00:08:07,951
Just hang in there a little longer! I know you're a strong bot!

168
00:08:09,600 --> 00:08:13,576
Ugh... Is this planet full of people who just don't know how to pick up on the vibe or what?

169
00:08:13,576 --> 00:08:16,074
Stop talking, Wild Cardbot.

170
00:08:16,074 --> 00:08:19,372
...Aaaaand the vibe is gone now. Way to be a killjoy!

171
00:08:19,372 --> 00:08:23,288
If you ever interrupt me again while I'm having fun, you'll pay dearly!

172
00:08:26,132 --> 00:08:30,680
Huh...? Why are you all looking at me like that?

173
00:08:30,680 --> 00:08:31,608
You endured well.

174
00:08:31,608 --> 00:08:32,792
Thankfully it wasn't too late.

175
00:08:32,792 --> 00:08:33,870
Thank goodness!

176
00:08:33,870 --> 00:08:35,787
Phoenix Fire...!!

177
00:08:35,787 --> 00:08:39,701
If we'd been just a moment too late, we could've been in big trouble. I never thought Night Griffon would appear so suddenly...

178
00:08:39,701 --> 00:08:41,961
Thank you, Crest. You too, Mega Ambler.

179
00:08:41,961 --> 00:08:42,575
Hm.

180
00:08:42,575 --> 00:08:45,153
You're the one who calls herself my twin sister, are you not?

181
00:08:45,153 --> 00:08:45,893
Huh?

182
00:08:45,893 --> 00:08:47,422
That's right, Crest.

183
00:08:47,422 --> 00:08:48,192
Mother!

184
00:08:48,192 --> 00:08:50,201
You mistook her for a stranger, didn't you?

185
00:08:50,201 --> 00:08:53,615
After all, she grew up to become such a beautiful young woman, you'd hardly even recognize her.

186
00:08:53,615 --> 00:08:55,738
Soleil, say hi to your big brother.

187
00:08:55,738 --> 00:08:57,363
It's been so long, big brother.

188
00:08:57,363 --> 00:08:59,118
Yeah. It has.

189
00:08:59,118 --> 00:09:03,331
If you don't mind, Soleil and I have some urgent errands to run. Let's go.

190
00:09:03,331 --> 00:09:05,350
Yes, mother.

191
00:09:05,750 --> 00:09:06,971
Goodbye...

192
00:09:06,971 --> 00:09:08,245
Blaion. Let's go.

193
00:09:08,245 --> 00:09:09,013
Hm.

194
00:09:09,413 --> 00:09:13,461
We'll see you kids again later! And good luck with that project of yours, my son!

195
00:09:14,379 --> 00:09:17,594
I need to head off as well. Jun, take care of Phoenix Fire for me.

196
00:09:17,594 --> 00:09:18,937
Uh, sure.

197
00:09:18,937 --> 00:09:20,293
Keep up the good work.

198
00:09:21,081 --> 00:09:22,960
Where's he going?

199
00:09:22,960 --> 00:09:26,234
To vaccinate everyone. Metal Cardbots all around town are waiting for him.

200
00:09:26,234 --> 00:09:27,379
It was completed?

201
00:09:27,379 --> 00:09:30,147
Then we no longer have to worry about the Beast Virus!

202
00:09:30,147 --> 00:09:32,504
I wish it were that easy... 

203
00:09:32,504 --> 00:09:37,163
But the vaccine needs to be administered before an infection. It's pointless to get it while already infected, as is the case now.

204
00:09:37,163 --> 00:09:38,619
Then what'll happen to Phoenix Fire?

205
00:09:38,619 --> 00:09:41,802
What we did for him is only a temporary measure to activate the nanomachines within his body

206
00:09:41,802 --> 00:09:44,385
to suppress physical changes and protect the thought processor circuit.

207
00:09:44,385 --> 00:09:47,451
Just in case, I think it's best to take him to my vacation home and monitor his progress.

208
00:09:47,451 --> 00:09:50,341
I have no idea what you just said... but okay.

209
00:09:51,043 --> 00:09:53,951
Really, now? Jun's Metal Cardbot told you that?

210
00:09:53,951 --> 00:09:58,392
I still do not understand. Why did he have to take such a drastic measure to save me?

211
00:09:58,392 --> 00:10:01,057
You also gave everything you had to help Blue Cop.

212
00:10:01,057 --> 00:10:06,158
I thought it would make you happy if I did it. You're very interested in Jun and Blue Cop.

213
00:10:06,158 --> 00:10:07,985
And I also took some samples from him.

214
00:10:07,985 --> 00:10:09,071
You did.

215
00:10:09,071 --> 00:10:13,888
But the Metal Cardbot who saved me risked his life simply because he thought Jun would be sad.

216
00:10:13,888 --> 00:10:16,754
"For your friends are my friends, and my friends are your friends." as the song goes.

217
00:10:16,754 --> 00:10:17,235
Excuse me?

218
00:10:17,235 --> 00:10:19,009
Hehe... It's nothing.

219
00:10:19,009 --> 00:10:20,671
I'm being serious.

220
00:10:20,671 --> 00:10:23,706
You already know that Jun refers to Metal Cardbots as his friends, right?

221
00:10:23,706 --> 00:10:24,581
Yes.

222
00:10:24,581 --> 00:10:27,721
Jun probably thinks of you as a dear friend, too. That's why-

223
00:10:27,721 --> 00:10:30,639
Are you saying he thinks I'm the same as the likes of those Metal Cardbots?!

224
00:10:33,662 --> 00:10:35,105
Soleil, are you alright?

225
00:10:35,105 --> 00:10:36,360
I-I'm sorry.

226
00:10:36,360 --> 00:10:37,913
Are you all right, ma'am?

227
00:10:37,913 --> 00:10:39,504
No need to worry about us, Garrison. 

228
00:10:39,504 --> 00:10:43,432
Thank goodness. I'll call the repair technician right away. Is there anything else?

229
00:10:43,432 --> 00:10:45,436
No. We're fine. Thank you.

230
00:10:46,134 --> 00:10:49,157
I didn't properly thank them yet.

231
00:10:49,157 --> 00:10:51,586
Me neither. I'd like to thank them for helping us.

232
00:10:51,586 --> 00:10:54,442
In that case, I'll teach you the perfect magic trick for that!

233
00:10:57,475 --> 00:11:00,048
That was really shocking yesterday...

234
00:11:00,950 --> 00:11:03,730
G... good morning...

235
00:11:03,730 --> 00:11:04,985
Hi! Good morning!

236
00:11:04,985 --> 00:11:06,542
G- good morning.

237
00:11:06,942 --> 00:11:07,557
Jun...

238
00:11:07,557 --> 00:11:09,224
Oh. Good morning.

239
00:11:09,224 --> 00:11:11,503
Thank you... for what you did yesterday.

240
00:11:11,503 --> 00:11:16,527
W-what's gotten into you? Say thank you to Phoenix Fire, not me.

241
00:11:18,216 --> 00:11:19,989
Turn your hand vertically...!

242
00:11:20,489 --> 00:11:25,466
We need to cooperate to catch Night Griffon. Please lend me your strength.

243
00:11:26,466 --> 00:11:27,668
Of course!

244
00:11:27,869 --> 00:11:28,998
Wha?! Did they just-

245
00:11:28,998 --> 00:11:29,647
-shake hands??

246
00:11:29,647 --> 00:11:30,615
Extra, extra!

247
00:11:30,716 --> 00:11:32,288
P-Please let go of my hand...

248
00:11:32,288 --> 00:11:34,201
You do realize that you were being super mean to me all this time, right?

249
00:11:34,201 --> 00:11:35,221
I'm sorry...

